G1611.b:
⟪ἔκ-στασις⟫, -εως, ἡ
(ἐξίστημι) [in LXX: ⟦Genesis 27:33|Ge 27:33⟧, ⟦1 Samuel 14:15|I Ki 14:15⟧, ⟦Ezekiel 26:16|Ez 26:16⟧, al. (⁨חֲרָדָה⁩); ⟦2 Chronicles 14:14|II Ch 14:14⟧ ⟦2 Chronicles 17:10|17:10⟧ ⟦2 Chronicles 20:29|20:29⟧ (⁨פַּחַד⁩), al. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a displacement⟫ (Arist.).
⟪2.⟫ An abnormal condition of the mind, in which the subject passes out of his usual self-control (Hippocr.); in NT (Kennedy, Sources, 121 f.);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a trance⟫: ⟦Acts 10:10|Ac 10:10⟧ ⟦Acts 11:5|11:5⟧ ⟦Acts 22:17|22:17⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪amazement⟫: ⟦Mark 5:42|Mk 5:42⟧ ⟦Mark 16:8|16:8⟧, ⟦Luke 5:26|Lk 5:26⟧, ⟦Acts 3:10|Ac 3:10⟧.†

G1623.b:
⟪ἐκτός⟫, adv.
[in LXX ⟦Judges 8:26|Jg 8:26⟧ ⟦Judges 20:15|20:15⟧, ⟦1 Kings 10:13|III Ki 10:13⟧, al. (⁨לִבַד מִן ,מִלְּבַד⁩, ⟦Judges 5:28|Jg 5:28⟧ (⁨בְּﬠַד⁩),⟦Song of Solomon 4:3|Ca 4:1-3⟧ (⁨מִבַּﬠַד לִִ⁩), al, ;]
⟪1.⟫ as adv., ⟪outside, beyond⟫: τὸ ἐ., c. poss. gen., ⟪the outside⟫, ⟦Matthew 23:26|Mt 23:26⟧; in late Gk. (v. Deiss., BS, 118), pleonastic, ἐκτός εἰ μή, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:5|I Co 14:5⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:2|15:2⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:19|I Ti 5:19⟧.
⟪2.⟫ With force of prep., c. gen.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪outside of⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 6:18|I Co 6:18⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:2|II Co 12:2⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪beyond, besides, except⟫: ⟦Acts 26:22|Ac 26:22⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:27|I Co 15:27⟧.†

G1627.b:
⟪ἐκ-φέρω⟫
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨יָצָא⁩ hi. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to carry out, bring out⟫: cc. acc rei, ⟦Luke 15:22|Lk 15:22⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:7|I Ti 6:7⟧; c. acc pers., ⟦Mark 8:23|Mk 8:23⟧, ⟦Acts 5:15|Ac 5:15⟧; of the dead for burial (cf. κομίζω), ⟦Acts 5:6|Ac 5:6⟧, ⟦Acts 5:9|9⟧, ⟦Acts 5:10|10⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to bring forth⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of women (Hipp., Arist., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ of the ground (Hdt.): ⟦Hebrews 6:8|He 6:8⟧.†

G1658.b:
⟪ἐλεύθερος⟫, -α, -ον
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨חׇפְשִׁי⁩ ;] ⟪free⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in civil sense, not a slave: ⟦John 8:33|Jo 8:33⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:21|I Co 7:21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:22|22⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 12:13|12:13⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:28|Ga 3:28⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:8|Eph 6:8⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:11|Col 3:11⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:15|Re 6:15⟧ ⟦Revelation 13:16|13:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 19:18|19:18⟧; fem., ⟦Galatians 4:22|Ga 4:22⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:23|23⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:30|30⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as regards restraint and obligation in general: ⟦Matthew 17:26|Mt 17:26⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:1|I Co 9:1⟧; seq. ἐκ, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:19|I Co 9:19⟧; ἀπό, ⟦Romans 7:3|Ro 7:3⟧; c. inf., ⟦1 Corinthians 7:39|I Co 7:39⟧; from the law, ⟦Galatians 4:26|Ga 4:26⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:16|I Pe 2:16⟧; from sin, ⟦John 8:36|Jo 8:36⟧; τῇ δικαιοσύνῃ, ⟪as regards righteousness⟫, ⟦Romans 6:20|Ro 6:20⟧ (Cremer, 249).†

G1680.b:
⟪ἐλπίς⟫
(ἑλ-, ⟦Romans 8:20|Ro 8:20⟧, WH, v. Bl., § 4, 3; M, Pr., 44), -ίδος, ἡ [in LXX for ⁨בָּטַח⁩ and its derivatives, ⁨תִּקְוָה⁩ (freq. in Jb), etc. ;] ⟪expectation⟫ (in cl., rarely of evil, mostly of good, and so always in NT), ⟪hope⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of hope in general: ⟦2 Corinthians 1:6|II Co 1:6⟧; c. gen. obj., ⟦Acts 16:19|Ac 16:19⟧; art. inf., ⟦Acts 27:20|Ac 27:20⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:10|I Co 9:10⟧; παρ’ ἐλπίδα, ⟦Romans 4:18|Ro 4:18⟧; ἐπ’ ἐλπίδι, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:10|I Co 9:10⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of religious hope: ἐπ’ ἐλπίδι, ⟦Acts 2:26|Ac 2:26⟧ ⟦Acts 26:6|26:6⟧, ⟦Romans 4:18|Ro 4:18⟧ ⟦Romans 8:20|8:20⟧, ⟦Titus 1:2|Tit 1:2⟧; τῇ ἐ. ἐσώθημεν, ⟦Romans 8:24|Ro 8:24⟧; κατ' ἐλπίδα ζωῆς αἰωνίου, ⟦Titus 3:7|Tit 3:7⟧; of the Messianic hope of Israel, ⟦Acts 23:6|Ac 23:6⟧ ⟦Acts 26:6|26:6⟧, ⟦Acts 26:7|7⟧ ⟦Acts 28:20|28:20⟧; of Christian hope, ⟦Romans 5:2|Ro 5:2⟧, ⟦Romans 5:4|4⟧, ⟦Romans 5:5|5⟧ ⟦Romans 12:12|12:12⟧ ⟦Romans 15:4|15:4⟧, ⟦Romans 15:13|13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 13:13|I Co 13:13⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:16|II Th 2:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:6|He 3:6⟧ ⟦Hebrews 6:11|6:11⟧ ⟦Hebrews 7:19|7:19⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:23|10:23⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:3|I Pe 1:3⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:21|21⟧ ⟦1 Peter 3:15|3:15⟧; c. gen. obj., ⟦Romans 5:2|Ro 5:2⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:27|Col 1:27⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 1:3|I Th 1:3⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:8|5:8⟧, ⟦Titus 1:2|Tit 1:2⟧; c. gen. of that on which the hope is based, ⟦Acts 26:6|Ac 26:6⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:18|Eph 1:18⟧ ⟦Ephesians 4:4|4:4⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:23|Col 1:23⟧; ὁ θεὸς τῆς ἐ., ⟦Romans 15:13|Ro 15:13⟧; ἔχειν ἐ. (= cl. ἐλπίζειν), ⟦Acts 24:15|Ac 24:15⟧, ⟦Romans 15:4|Ro 15:4⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:12|II Co 3:12⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 10:15|10:15⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:12|Eph 2:12⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:13|I Th 4:13⟧; seq. ἐπί, c. dat., ⟦1 John 3:3|I Jo 3:3⟧; εἰς, ⟦Acts 24:15|Ac 24:15⟧; ὅτι, ⟦Romans 8:20|Ro 8:20⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:20|Phl 1:20⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:21|21⟧. Meton.,
⟪(a)⟫ of the author or ground of hope (cl.): ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 1:1|I Ti 1:1⟧; c. gen. obj., ⟦Colossians 1:27|Col 1:27⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of the thing hoped for: ⟦Galatians 5:5|Ga 5:5⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:5|Col 1:5⟧, ⟦Titus 2:13|Tit 2:13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:18|He 6:18⟧ (Cremer, 252, 712).†

G1690.b:
⟪ἐμ-βριμάομαι⟫ (T, -έομαι; Bl., § 22, 1), -ῶμαι
(< βρίμη, ⟪strength, bulk⟫, whence βριμάομαι, ⟪to snort with anger⟫), depon., with aor. mid. and pass.,
[in LXX (Hatch, Essays, 25): ⟦Daniel 11:30|Da LXX 11:30⟧ (also Aq., ⟦Psalms 7:12|Ps 7:12⟧; Sm., ⟦Isaiah 17:13|Is 17:13⟧) * ;] ⟪to snort in⟫ (of horses, Æsch.), hence, to speak or act with deep feeling (DCG, i, 62b);
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to be moved with anger⟫ (cf. ἐμβρίμημα, ⟦Lamentations 2:6|La 2:6⟧): c. dat., ⟦Mark 14:5|Mk 14:5⟧, ⟦John 11:33|Jo 11:33⟧; ἐν ἑαυτῷ, ⟦John 11:38|Jo 11:38⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to admonish sternly⟫: c. dat., ⟦Matthew 9:30|Mt 9:30⟧, ⟦Mark 1:43|Mk 1:43⟧.†
